    "name": "Chain",
    "projectionMode": 1,
    "renderMode": 1,
    "scriptCode": "// --- A CHAIN OF FIVE LINKS ---\n// Five rings along x, each one turned by 90 degrees with respect to the next\n// and close enough to pass through it. `mesh` (0..4) sets the place along\n// the chain and the plane of the ring.\n//MESH_BEGIN\nu: 0, TAU, 200\nv: 0, TAU, 32\n//MESH_END\n//MESH_BEGIN\nu: 0, TAU, 200\nv: 0, TAU, 32\n//MESH_END\n//MESH_BEGIN\nu: 0, TAU, 200\nv: 0, TAU, 32\n//MESH_END\n//MESH_BEGIN\nu: 0, TAU, 200\nv: 0, TAU, 32\n//MESH_END\n//MESH_BEGIN\nu: 0, TAU, 200\nv: 0, TAU, 32\n//MESH_END\nfloat cx = (mesh - 2.0) * 1.3;\nvec3 c = vec3(cx + 1.0*cos(u), sin(u), 0.0);\nif (mod(mesh, 2.0) > 0.5) c = vec3(cx + cos(u), 0.0, sin(u));\nreturn vec4(c * 0.6, 0.0);\n",
